<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dongcheon of Goguryeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 227–248</span> · Also known as King Dongcheon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dongcheon was the eleventh king of Goguryeo, reigning from 227 to 248. He allied with the Chinese state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a> against the Gongsun warlords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> but then attacked Wei territory in 242. In 244–245 the Wei general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanqiu-jian">Guanqiu Jian</a> invaded, sacked the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hwando">Hwando</a> and forced the king to flee to the Okjeo lands, though Goguryeo soon recovered.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dongcheon-of-goguryeo.jpg" alt="Dongcheon of Goguryeo" width="300" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ja:user:田英 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goguryeo-monarchs(6-11).PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
